# Design Engineering Routing

When the task materially changes what a user sees, understands, navigates or
does—UX/UI, information architecture, visual hierarchy, dashboards/admin shells,
design systems, interaction, responsive behavior, accessibility behavior,
motion, branding or interface critique—route Senior -> Frontend -> Design and
read `.engineer-intelligence/senior/frontend/design/SKILL.md` plus
`.engineer-intelligence/runtime/design/DESIGN-DELIVERY-CONTRACT-V1.0.md` for
substantial work.

Design is not a root sibling of Frontend. Activate it only when the requested
work changes user-visible behavior or makes a design decision. Never activate it
from file location, directory name, route name, or workspace layout alone. For a
code-only bug fix without a design decision, stay on the normal frontend route.
A media query or static DOM result is not rendered responsive or interaction
evidence.

For native mobile screen/flow work, pair Design with Frontend -> Mobile and read
`.engineer-intelligence/senior/frontend/design/mobile-interface/SKILL.md`. For
production websites, UI critique, or motion review, load the matching
web-production, UI-quality, or motion-quality context and its targeted upstream
skill; prefer its mirrored `.cursor/skills/<skill-name>/SKILL.md` entry when
installed, with the preserved canonical source under
`.engineer-intelligence/knowledge/ai-web-design-skills-v1.0.0/.claude/skills/`
as the fallback. Do not load every industry profile by default.
